        <strong>Full Names:</strong> New Zealand Standard Time (NZST) / New Zealand Daylight Time (NZDT)  
        <br /><strong>Winter Offset:</strong> UTC+12  
        <br /><strong>Summer Offset:</strong> UTC+13  
        <br /><strong>Major Cities:</strong> Auckland, Wellington, Christchurch.  
        <br /><strong>Usage Note:</strong> Observed in New Zealand. Clocks shift on the last Sunday of September and the first Sunday of April.
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- PST / PDT -->
    <article class="method-card" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h3>PST &amp; PDT</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Full Names:</strong> Pacific Standard Time (PST) / Pacific Daylight Time (PDT)  
        <br /><strong>Winter Offset:</strong> UTC-8  
        <br /><strong>Summer Offset:</strong> UTC-7  
        <br /><strong>Major Cities:</strong> Los Angeles, San Francisco, Seattle, Vancouver, Las Vegas.  
        <br /><strong>Usage Note:</strong> Observed in western North America.
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- WET / WEST -->
    <article class="method-card" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h3>WET &amp; WEST</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Full Names:</strong> Western European Time (WET) / Western European Summer Time (WEST)  
        <br /><strong>Winter Offset:</strong> UTC+0  
        <br /><strong>Summer Offset:</strong> UTC+1  
        <br /><strong>Major Cities:</strong> Lisbon, Funchal, Las Palmas.  
        <br /><strong>Usage Note:</strong> Observed in Portugal (mainland), Canary Islands, and Faroe Islands.
