  <section id="business-scheduling" class="content-section reveal" aria-label="Business Operations &amp; Meeting Coordination">
    <h2>5. Business Operations &amp; Meeting Coordination</h2>
    <p>
      Coordinating international corporate activities requires matching standard and daylight abbreviations to establish clear communication corridors.
    </p>

    <!-- Visual Asset 10: Business Meeting Illustration -->
    <figure style="margin: 2.5rem 0; text-align: center; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--panel);">
      <img 
        src="/assets/business-meeting-abbreviations.webp" 
        alt="Global Team Meeting Coordinator Matrix showing overlaps across PDT, EDT, and BST" 
        title="Business Meeting Illustration" 
        loading="lazy" 
        decoding="async" 
        width="800" 
        height="400" 
        style="width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 8px;"
      />
      <figcaption class="infographic-caption">
        <strong>Figure 10: Multi-Timezone Collaboration.</strong> Matrix demonstrating working hour overlaps between PDT, EDT, and BST for remote teams.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>PDT, EDT, and BST Overlap:</strong> During summer, a meeting scheduled at 9:00 a.m. in San Francisco (PDT, UTC-7) corresponds to 12:00 p.m. in New York (EDT, UTC-4) and 5:00 p.m. in London (BST, UTC+1). 
        This represents the optimal daily collaboration window for trans-Atlantic corporate teams.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Daylight Saving Transitions:</strong> Clocks in North America (switching EST to EDT) change on different dates compared to Europe (switching CET to CEST). 
        During the 2-to-3 week gap in March and October, meeting times will shift by one hour, requiring close attention.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Half-Hour Offsets:</strong> When scheduling calls with India (IST, UTC+5:30) or Newfoundland (NST, UTC-3:30), meetings scheduled on the hour in standard zones will land on the half-hour in these regions, making careful calendar booking essential.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

